          <item>Use the sum of the first $$10$$ terms to estimate the sum of the series $$\sum_{n = 1}^{\infty}{1 \slash n^{2}}$$ . How good is this estimate?</item>
          <item>Improve this estimate using (3) with $$n = 10$$ .</item>
          <item>Compare your estimate in part (b) with the exact value given in Exercise 36.</item>
          <item>Find a value of $$n$$ that will ensure that the error in the approximation $$s \approx s_{n}$$ is less than $$0.001$$ .</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1.54977$$ , $${error} \leqslant 0.1$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>$$1.64522$$ , $${error} \leqslant 0.005$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>$$1.64522$$ compared to $$1.64493$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>$$n &gt; 1000$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
